VESION FILE - RCLONE-WIZ


All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file from now on.

[1.3] - 2026-06-07

Added
Dynamic Script Management: Introduced a dedicated ~/.config/rclone-wiz/ directory, allowing users to save and manage individual mount scripts for multiple cloud remotes simultaneously.

Legacy Migration Support: Implemented an automatic detection system to identify and migrate legacy scripts from ~/rclone_mount_script.sh to the new configuration directory upon saving.

Added os.path.ismount() checks to prevent FUSE errors when attempting to mount over existing active mount points.

Added a "Load Existing Script" button to auto-populate fields based on existing configuration files.

Added informative status hints to the UI to notify users when a drive is already mounted.

State Synchronization: Implemented signal blocking for input fields to prevent recursive triggers and UI conflicts when loading existing scripts.

UX Refinements: Standardized the GUI layout with improved spacing and visual indicators for load/migration states.

Fixed
FUSE Overlap Prevention: Implemented automatic clearing of the "Mount Path" field when switching between different remotes to ensure users do not accidentally target an incorrect or currently mounted directory.

Concurrency Handling: Refined background worker thread logic to ensure cleaner process termination and unmount sequences.


[1.4] - 2026-06-08

Added
Enhanced VFS Caching: Updated the generated mount script to include optimized VFS caching parameters, such as --vfs-cache-max-size, --vfs-cache-max-age, and --buffer-size, to improve performance when streaming media files from cloud storage.
Added --fast-list and --poll-interval options to the mount script for faster directory listing and more responsive updates when changes occur in the cloud storage.
Added comments in the generated script to explain the purpose of each rclone option for better user understanding

